r/validate]} {:db/id "q-340652/field-3/a90aeb19f2ec5a1bc25ecfb9d128f7b45fcf3ecc2ca1da37beda3de810f14649" :answer/id #uuid "ed316cc8-07b3-50f0-b68d-1e3c4f94af83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340652/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "759f0e80-461e-5d3d-b64a-f23a8617fd32" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-340652/field-3/d41d770c9dfc4786623b2439c5d063f14747710accefa6bd9d7ebb33f696e98c" :answer-field/choices ["q-340652/field-3/67306f195dd5c9d3952fda8ad16def89350be707ef23db7f1ac9fe874ffdf37a" "q-340652/field-3/97f25bcc4138e5e5c32bdd3a0a7aa85c0e1577cd28a63f8e6f3bb41e704ff400" "q-340652/field-3/12afd28716ef2d7b736944b01510278cc054caddde4b34461b47cc2431de23c5" "q-340652/field-3/2e16d33745785a5a5e1ce29e4805701d2f15f0f3f8d12289bd37d3e55e0b1958" "q-340652/field-3/d41d770c9dfc4786623b2439c5d063f14747710accefa6bd9d7ebb33f696e98c" "q-340652/field-3/a90aeb19f2ec5a1bc25ecfb9d128f7b45fcf3ecc2ca1da37beda3de810f14649"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340652" :question/id #uuid "b0b4bc13-295e-5cd6-bfe3-3a43c6627cde" :question/math-academy-id "q-340652" :question/problem "Let $F(x)={x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${b}_{1}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that's piecewise continuous over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi -(-\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi ))) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩ & ={b}_{1}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩ \\\\ {b}_{1} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩} \\\\ {b}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340652/field-1" "q-340652/field-2" "q-340652/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "304c015d-cbb6-5989-a102-d6f0f5f38604"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340652"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-341340/field-1/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" :answer/id #uuid "c1f85280-8e69-5725-84b3-4e2ab7513f5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341340/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "889ca4ec-1d7c-535a-9022-621ac18d4863" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341340/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "bcb08248-d559-571b-87fc-91e35ee54b85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341340/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "d88a5898-98df-5333-bc4a-be16b88e205b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341340/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "46fcd125-ed9f-586c-a5c5-1f7d8614f8ae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-341340/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-341340/field-1/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" "q-341340/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-341340/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-341340/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341340/field-2/45748e934ef4660a4b62ead5bf1f91dfb438725115d7289eb41fe950d2ed803d" :answer/id #uuid "14deddee-2075-5648-b7ad-fe08270547b8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341340/field-2/61bbf40bf0728127bc167767b5af83361c3acbddac67f4a51d278c010c10af58" :answer/id #uuid "742fb714-53d1-5467-ae56-4a16fca7500d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "are not orthogonal" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341340/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "6392ce22-722f-5d8c-9e58-313b05f5bdae" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-341340/field-2/45748e934ef4660a4b62ead5bf1f91dfb438725115d7289eb41fe950d2ed803d" :answer-field/choices ["q-341340/field-2/45748e934ef4660a4b62ead5bf1f91dfb438725115d7289eb41fe950d2ed803d" "q-341340/field-2/61bbf40bf0728127bc167767b5af83361c3acbddac67f4a51d278c010c10af58"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341340" :question/id #uuid "0593ec7c-7f2e-54b5-93d7-d18f56e360e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-341340" :question/problem "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ defined above, select the correct options below.$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)⟩=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We begin by using the product-to-sum identity\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{14}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(14\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))+\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}(1-1)+\\frac{1}{2}(1-1) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-341340/field-1" "q-341340/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fadf4f64-3569-56b2-98e1-f6681892054a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341340"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
